{# ===========================================================================
   Component: location-menu

   Section 4 of the location page template in SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md: this
   room's menu, from menu.json filtered by `locations`, linking to /menu/.

   REBUILT TWICE, 2026-09-14. It was a plain grouped list of names, then the
   B2 module (a three-column list, no photography), and it is now A2, a port of
   _reference/menu-concepts/tajima-ev-menu-A2.html: the same three columns with
   a 92px square photograph beside every dish. One component drives this and
   the concept routes, so a location page and a review route cannot drift.

   PHOTOGRAPHY IS SCOPED TO THE ROOM. The module reads _data/dishPhotos.js,
   which only returns a photograph whose filename names this location, which is
   photos.json's `_rule`. Measured 2026-09-14: Convoy has 13 of its 14 dishes
   photographed and Maui 4 of its 8; Mercury, East Village, College Heights,
   Crown Point and Plaza Bonita have no dish photography of their own at all
   and render the reference's placeholder tile on every card. That is the shoot
   that has happened, not a fault in this component, and borrowing Convoy's
   frames to fill it would break the rule the whole manifest is built on.

   USAGE
     {% set menuLoc = loc.id %}
     {% include "components/location-menu.njk" %}

   NO PRICES. /menu/ prints none as of 2026-09-10 and the client has not ruled
   on location pages. Per-room prices DO exist and are complete: every
   featured dish at every room has a live price in that room's own
   toastMenus/*.json. Turning them on here is a data decision, not a template
   change. See the report and menuConcepts.json `_prices`.

   A room whose filter returns nothing for every section renders nothing at
   all rather than an empty module. Nothing currently hits that, but Maui is
   the thinnest at seven rows and no dessert.
   =========================================================================== #}
{%- set mcAny = (menu.items | dishesFor(menuLoc, "ramen") | length)
              + (menu.items | dishesFor(menuLoc, "izakaya") | length)
              + (menu.items | dishesFor(menuLoc, "dessert") | length) %}
{%- if mcAny %}
{#- id="menu" IS LOAD-BEARING, 2026-09-15. /menu/ is a room chooser now, so a
    "See the menu" link on a room page that points there asks a reader standing
    in Convoy to pick a room. Six links across the NAP plate, both full location
    templates, the stub and the Maui order close now point at #menu instead,
    which is this section, on the page they are already on. -#}
<section class="sect mc-sect" id="menu" aria-label="Menu at this location">
  <div class="sect__inner">
    <div class="mc mc--inline">
      {%- set mcLoc = menuLoc %}
      {%- set mcChrome = false %}
      {#- A2 is what ships.  exists for the internal A/B route at
      /internal/menu-a2-vs-b2/ and nothing else sets it; real location pages
      always get the default. -#}
      {#- A2 is what ships. `mcVariantOverride` exists for the internal A/B route
          at /internal/menu-a2-vs-b2/ and nothing else sets it, so a real
          location page always gets the default. -#}
      {%- set variant = mcVariantOverride | default("a2") %}
      {%- set showPrices = false %}
      {% include "components/menu-concept.njk" %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
